 "summary": "Host-only. Built reproducibly (two builds, identical SHA-256) a XNU-free AArch64 framebuffer-marker canary (plain and BRK-fault variants) and an instrumented derivative of the NAT-020 build-003 loader whose silent MMU/cache/EL halts report on the framebuffer. 12 host tests run the real marker C code against a RAM buffer and an independent Python decoder; make check passed 214 tests. The AArch64 assembly start path was assembled/linked but never executed (no AArch64 emulator on this host) and nothing ran on the phone: framebuffer scanout at 0xFA200000, pixel order, stride and the true halt location remain unknown. A concrete owner decision request is in docs/procedures/nat-022/README.md; no native action was taken or authorised.",
